Subject: [#94-5-178] Phase change on the net (was: Filtering Techniques)

On Tue, 3 May 1994, R Bryner wrote:
> Again, this is adding information, not censorship.  I think the value of
> such a meta-list could eventualy become one of the hotest comodities.

I've been predicting for a couple months now that this kind of thing is 
about to become a growth industry on the Net.  I think two factors will 
trigger the explosive growth phase: the commercenet secure mosaic 
software to enable secure money transactions, and a credit card brokerage 
service built on top of it that will allow people to receive money 
without themselves having to become authorized to accept credit card 
payment.

Of course, there are a lot of other services that will see an explosive 
growth phase at about that same time . . . .

I heard a gentleman from EIT speak about secure mosaic and CommerceNet.  
Two very interesting items: the secure mosaic code will be included in a 
free (and royalty free) release of the standard WWW library, and 
CommerceNet has several large finnancial institutions, including CityBank 
and the Bank of Boston, *very* interested in electronic banking on the Net.

The plan is for the freely distributable versions of the software to be 
released to the Net by the end of the summer.

I'd say the Internet is about to experience a phase change . . . or 
rather an accelleration of the one that is already occuring.

--David


