[ I suggest that we rename the threads once in a while, to reflect content]   
 
 
   I doubt that making decisions in 1 seconds instead of 5 does any good
for the market at this point; economy is [still] too slow, and nothing is
going to happen to it in a few seconds.  
So it's just a new way greedy capitalists can steal money from each other :)
 
   The real advantages of faster trading now may be in side-effects:
higher transaction speeds require superior information technology, and both
the technology and the financial markets benefit from this alliance in a
variety of ways.
 
   Maybe, some day the rate of economic processes will catch up with the
speed of information processing.  By that time, the information may be the
only economic output.
 
